  "text": "```python\ndef binary_search(a, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Perform binary search on a sorted list `a` for the target value `x`.\n    \n    Args:\n        a: A sorted list of comparable elements.\n        x: The target value to search for.\n    \n    Returns:\n        The index of `x` in `a` if found, otherwise -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(a) - 1\n    \n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if a[mid] == x:\n            return mid\n        elif a[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    \n    return -1\n\n\n# Tests\ndef test_binary_search():\n    # Test empty list\n    assert binary_search([], 5) == -1\n    \n    # Test missing item\n    assert binary_search([1, 3, 5, 7, 9], 4) == -1\n    \n    # Test found item\n    assert binary_search([1, 3, 5, 7, 9], 5)",
